{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-19T07:09:40.574Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Implemented the approval-run manifest.**\n\n- **`src/core/manifest.ts`** (new, 138 lines): exports `ManifestData`, `buildManifest`, and `writeManifest`, with private helpers for config discovery, SHA-256 hashing, version, model, and created-at resolution.\n- **`src/core/approve.ts`**: calls `buildManifest`/`writeManifest` after the `approved` marker is written, producing `<change>/.run/manifest.json`.\n- **`tests/manifest.test.ts`** (new): verifies hashes for `AGENTS.md`, `PLANNER.md`, `config`, and each `features.reads`/`features.writes` spec, plus metadata and the `null`-on-missing-file case.\n\n**One deliberate deviation:** the task Details said to import `resolveBuildInfo` from `../watcher/build.js`, but that breaks the living `watcher-and-harness` *Architectural import graph boundaries* requirement (core may only import core) enforced by `tests/import-graph.test.ts`, and `src/watcher/build.ts` is outside the task scope. I implemented an equivalent local `resolveOsqVersion` inside `manifest.ts` instead. This is documented in the result file.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/manifest.test.ts` → 2/2 pass\n- `pnpm verify` (tsc + 559 tests + lint) → all pass\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/026-raw-measures-and-run-manifest/.run/results/1.md`. Next up is task 2 (measures event at task start)."}}
